 { Position 13.3 is the most remarkable. The barrier set up by bishop and knight is impossible to cross and the black king is locked in a cage. Thus White can play with total calm. Interestingly, this position can arise in a normal sequence of play following the usual mating procedure, and the best thing is that the shortest mating manoeuvre leads to this position without wasting time. You do not have to memorise these positions, it is enough to read the comments and have another look at the diagrams every time there is a reference to one of them. Now we are going to see an example. We will follow the classical procedure, although Deletang's Method (Deletang's Triangles) is also very valuable. Actually, diagrams 13.1 and 13.3 are intermediate stages in Deletang's Method: these are the large and the middle triangle. I do not advise you to study two methods, but you should observe carefully Position 13.1 and understand that this disposition of pieces may be useful in the initial stage, that, is, cornering the enemy king. }  
